  id: "hw-first-host",
  workstream: Hardware,
  milestone: M1InternalVertical,
  rank: 10,
  min_calendar_days: 14,
  active_effort_days: 14,
  execution_mode: OperatorExclusive,
  exit_criterion: "Unit 1 through intake phases 1-5: FRU'd, BMC recredentialed, memtest pass, Linux EDAC pass clean (nproc 160), DIMM population matches the J-slot table - one held-unit receipt module. ONE admitted host is the M1 canary; the other three do not gate the vertical.",
  depends_on: no_deps,
  relates_to: ["strategy.mt_collins_held_unit", "strategy.ci_node_build"],
  item_relations: no_item_relations,
  status: InProgress { note: "FOUR OF FIVE INTAKE PHASES DISCHARGED, AS TYPED STEPS IN strategy.owner_action: FRU, BMC probe and memtest (receipt_hw1_intake_phases_1_3); the J-slot census (receipt_hw1_jslot_census, public gunbc#10965: sixteen 16 GB modules with part and serial per slot, one per channel on all sixteen channels, corroborated pre-OS by the firmware DRAM table in gunbc#11189 -- so filling the empty slots is a 2DPC capacity change at a data-rate cost, not free bandwidth, and a 32-module mixed population was firmware-refused, gunbc#11110); and the BMC recredential (receipt_hw1_bmc_recredential, public gunbc#11234: factory admin RETIRED, managed account from Secret Manager bmc-mtcollins1-gunbc). THE ONE OPEN STEP IS step_hw1_edac_pass: no host has booted to Linux since the module swap -- the restore evidence ends at the UEFI shell for want of boot media, and the public pre-OS model reads that as undetermined (gunbc#11189 mtcollins1_restore_positive_terminal_frontier). Its route is the modeled virtual-media boot (gunbc#10630; the diskless image is already published on srv2's export), which cannot authenticate until the rotated credential is reachable from the modeled operations -- public gunbc.machine_intake_bmc_secure mtcollins1_bmc_secure_standing_frontier, in flight as eager-owl-205's child lane 2026-09-16." },
}

data item_boot_minimum: PlanItem = PlanItem {
  id: "boot-minimum",
  workstream: Hardware,
  milestone: M1InternalVertical,
  rank: 20,
  min_calendar_days: 5,
  active_effort_days: 5,
  execution_mode: AgentParallel,
  exit_criterion: "The M1 boot property WITHOUT the full netboot product: deterministic digest-identified host image, no durable customer state on the boot device, BMC-driven unattended reinstall/reset with a measured host-reset receipt, short-lived runtime credentials, boot device treated as disposable. Production diskless netboot moves to netboot-m0 (M2b) - it can slip without invalidating the demo.",
  depends_on: [dep(id: "hw-first-host")],
  relates_to: ["strategy.mobo_x_architecture"],
  item_relations: [RemainderLivesOn { of: "netboot-m0", why: "Production diskless netboot may slip without invalidating the M1 demo; this item holds the security property meanwhile." }],
  status: InProgress { note: "Transport PROVEN, boot-minimum NOT closed. Observed on the real machine: boots Linux over PXE (nproc 160, EDAC clean, dmidecode -t memory); the repo-built stateless host image boots; switch_root to tmpfs gives a RAM-backed runtime root; the stock Firecracker jailer is traversed and runs as uid 1000 in a chroot plus namespaces; /dev/kvm opens from inside the jail and a guest kernel is reached under KVM; the host deadline fires, nothing survives, the jail is removed. Receipts in gunbc#10733, on main at c9ef79fdeea. THE BOOT ROUTE: gunbc#10630 (2026-09-10) made fetch, digest verification, publication into the export, MegaRAC virtual-media attach and boot-device handoff modeled operations with typed refusals, executed against the live controller; it is DISKLESS, NOT RAM-RESIDENT (casper toram absent), and it does not touch PXE, so netboot-m0's PXE-E16 blocker stands. TWO CONJUNCTS REMAIN and neither is transport. (1) BMC-driven unattended reinstall with a MEASURED RESET RECEIPT: the model merged as gunbc#10739 (51 witnesses) has never executed. Its blocker has CHANGED SHAPE, not gone: the pinned credential now EXISTS (Secret Manager bmc-mtcollins1-gunbc; factory admin retired, strategy.owner_action receipt_hw1_bmc_recredential) but no modeled BMC operation can reach it -- the username rows on the media-attach and handoff operations still name the retired account, and public gunbc.machine_intake_bmc_secure carries the unit-1 subject + SecretRef binding as its frontier (in flight, eager-owl-205's child lane 2026-09-16). Until it lands, every helper that authenticated as admin/admin fails. (2) Root mount identity before and after switch_root is still ahead of its evidence. NEW SINCE 09-10: the unit went through a 32-DIMM restart loop and a firmware-refused 3DS mixture and is restored to sixteen modules; the host has not been booted to Linux since." },
}

// ADDED 2026-09-07 on operator instruction. This requirement was live and being tracked OUTSIDE
// the plan -- it sat on the operator's own working list as "no accounts yet, create ASAP" while
// fabric-m0 declared no dependencies and therefore read as startable. That is exactly what
// requirement_coalescence_note forbids: a requirement discovered later is added HERE as an item,
// never tracked in a side list, because an item the plan cannot see cannot be late. Two providers
// rather than one is not redundancy -- the durable origin's whole claim is a failure domain
// disjoint from the worker, and a single provider account is a single point of both failure and
// commercial leverage. It is OperatorExclusive because payment instrument, legal entity and
// region are the operator's to bind, and because none of that is delegable to an agent.
// ADDED 2026-09-07 on operator instruction ("we need buyer agents ... there is no deterministic
// filtering on ebay, too many wrong accounts"), then NARROWED the same day by the operator to the
// scope this row now carries: scan the API listings, produce a sheet for manual review, and commit
// a typed intent to buy after that review. The narrowing is what makes this a two-week item rather
// than a programme -- with a human reading the sheet, the agent does not have to DECIDE fit, only
// to SURFACE the evidence, and deciding fit from unreliable listings was the hard half.
//
// IT INHERITS THE EXISTING PIPELINE RATHER THAN RESTARTING IT. strategy.buyers_pipeline already
// carries DemandRow, ListingObservation, propose(), the viability ceiling and the verified-depth
// refusal, and its scout contract already rules that THE SCOUT NEVER ACTUATES A PURCHASE. This row
// adds the three things that contract names but nothing produces: a cited upstream to read from, a
// projection the operator can actually review, and a typed intent that survives the review.
//
// THE FAILURE THIS MUST NOT REPRODUCE, because a spreadsheet is where it hides best: an attribute
// the listing never stated must not reach the sheet as a blank cell, because a blank reads as
// nothing-to-see and an unstated ECC field is exactly the cell the operator needs to stop on. An
// absence rendered as a value is the same defect the cost-account and actuator-selection lanes were
// closing this week, and a review sheet is its most natural habitat.
data item_buyer_agent_pipeline: PlanItem = PlanItem {
  id: "buyer-agent-pipeline",
  workstream: Hardware,
  milestone: M1bInternalS0Proof,
  rank: 10,
  min_calendar_days: 14,
  active_effort_days: 14,
  execution_mode: AgentParallel,
  exit_criterion: "SCAN, SHEET, INTENT - and no actuation. (1) The marketplace is a cited upstream with its own extdeps module under the external-decomposition rule: API version, the endpoints read, the published rate limits, and the fields a listing payload ACTUALLY returns, so the sheet's columns are derived from the API's response shape rather than invented. (2) A scheduled run turns those responses into ListingObservation rows against buyer_demand_rows and projects them to a review sheet GENERATED FROM THE MODEL, never hand-assembled - a hand-authored projection of something the model can emit is the tell that the model is not the authority. The sheet ranks by the spread between delivered unit price and the row's viability ceiling, and every compatibility attribute renders three-valued: stated and corroborated by part number or photograph, stated only, or ABSENT AND SAID TO BE ABSENT. A blank cell for an unstated attribute is the defect, not the format. (3) After the operator reviews, a PurchaseIntent is COMMITTED TO THE CORPUS as a typed row - demand row, listing identity, units, delivered unit price, the attributes accepted on the operator's judgement rather than on evidence, and the intake obligation it triggers - so what was decided is readable later rather than living in a chat message. NOT owed and deliberately so: purchase actuation, which the scout contract keeps human by design; any scraping, since the agent reads the published API as a signed-in buyer; and automatic fit adjudication, which the manual review replaces for now and which becomes owed only if sheet volume makes reading every row impractical.",
  depends_on: no_deps,
  relates_to: ["strategy.buyers_pipeline", "strategy.procurement_order", "strategy.ci_node_build"],
  item_relations: no_item_relations,
  status: InProgress { note: "SCAN AND OBSERVE HALF LANDED as gunbc-private#92, merged 2026-09-13T00:30:34Z, with the sheet projection half owned separately by the Google Sheets lane and bound rather than duplicated. Rates joined to first-party region reads; supply on every joined row stays Unobserved so admissible_as_competitive_floor remains false - a region join is NOT a supply observation and the flag must not flip because a rate found a region. REMAINDER CORRECTED 2026-09-13 against origin/main, because the previous sentence named ALREADY-LANDED work as outstanding: it claimed the marketplace extdeps module and the three-valued compatibility rendering were the remainder, and both exist. strategy.buyer_review_sheet imports extdeps.ebay.inventory, extdeps.ebay.browse and extdeps.ebay.rate_limits, and attribute_cell renders SEVEN arms rather than three - AttributeCorroborated, AttributeImpliedByPartNumber, AttributeContradicted, AttributeStatedOnly, AttributeStatedAmbiguously, AttributeAbsent and AttributeAlternativesUnresolved - and since gunbc-private#95 also the package-type axis, typed lot uniformity and DemandQuantityStanding. WHAT IS ACTUALLY OUTSTANDING, each verified rather than asserted: (1) the eBay scan was gated on ebay-exemption-applicability, then ebay-retention-permitted, then ebay-browse-scheduled-scan. ebay-retention-permitted was DISCHARGED 2026-09-18 by an operator risk acceptance (strategy.gunbc_strategy decision_ebay_retention_permitted, typed facts in ebay_retention_risk_limitations: dedicated seller identity unwritable, free-text title/URL/item specifics unpoliced, eBay adjudication absent, residual risk owned by the operator). ebay-exemption-applicability REMAINS OPEN -- the ruling authorizes retention without answering it -- so the remaining gate on the scan is ebay-browse-scheduled-scan itself, which is agent work; (2) NO RamPurchaseStanding ARM ESTABLISHES A QUANTITY - the type has exactly two arms, RamHeldCensusIdentityGap and RamHeldQualificationGap, and its own annotation states both are HELD and neither establishes a fleet RAM quantity, so the RDIMM and NVMe rows stay Unestablished by construction; (3) the Mt Collins remainder carries no demand warrant - test.claim.buyers_pipeline_witness asserts propose over demand_mt_collins returns ProposalRefusedQuantityUnestablished at candidate_units 0, blocked on a purchase record that does not establish it; (4) a Micron DS/SF part-number decoder in the PUBLIC extdeps.memory.micron, which EXISTS on public main carrying the part catalog and the 2018-12-05 part-numbering revision as cited authorities but no decoding function - so this is a decoder added to an existing module, not a new module. AND NO ACTUATION EXISTS OR IS AUTHORIZED - nothing bids, offers, buys or messages a seller. WIND-DOWN POSITION 2026-09-20 (operator: all work winding down, priority moves to v1 performance and v2 migration; recorded here so the chain resumes from the row, not from memory). The SHEET half's live-write lane is documented end to end in docs/plans/ebay-buyer-sheet-live-write-handoff.md, which is the authority for what follows. LANDED, public gunbc: #11589 (the public buyer-schema fork deleted), #11703 (one A1 sheet-title codec; always quotes, REFUSES an apostrophe title), #11705 (ValidatedHeaderSchema sole_constructor, and a live off-by-one fixed in the format band and Standing column), #11717 (all-or-nothing lowering, ONE BatchUpdateValues, fresh whole-tab reassessment, success only on WriteVerifiedConverged), #11725 (located-tab authority; replaced a first-sheet constant AND a readback that took the head of the sheet list), #11747. LANDED, private: #154 (the retention ruling recorded as an operator RISK ACCEPTANCE under acknowledged uncertainty, with four typed limitations as required fields -- NOT a finding that no personal data is stored), #155, #161 (H1: srv1 admission, sealed execution identity, fixed hold root, host-gated recovery whose release needs a sealed warrant). IN FLIGHT: gunbc#11769 (formula-preserving emptiness carrier; the side chat's hold is implemented at head 10afa61 and awaiting its ruling; 9 of 21 mutation rows run at that head, 12 carried from 5a2eaaa with byte-identical subjects). REMAINING, in order: finish #11769; build H2, the private locked live transaction strategy.buyer_review_live, in the order the side chat ruled; create /var/lib/gunbc/buyer-review/holds on srv1 with restrictive owner and mode; run the live qualification that a temporary tab holding a blank-rendering formula reads OCCUPIED under FORMULA and yields no write permit and no mutation; settle operator quiescence before any unattended timer, because the hold excludes automated writers and not a human editing in the browser; decompose ebay-browse-scheduled-scan before claiming any part of it, since it has no halves; and census strategy.ci_prospect_sheet_write before deleting converge_sheet_values. STILL OPEN AND UNCHANGED: ebay-exemption-applicability -- eBay has not adjudicated whether the disclosed retention falls within the filed exemption, and the operator's risk acceptance authorizes retention without answering it." }
}

data item_storage_provider_accounts: PlanItem = PlanItem {
  id: "storage-provider-accounts",
  workstream: StorageFabric,
  milestone: M1InternalVertical,
  rank: 5,
  min_calendar_days: 3,
  active_effort_days: 3,
  execution_mode: OperatorExclusive,
  exit_criterion: "Accounts live at BOTH candidate object-storage providers (Cloudflare R2 and Backblaze B2), American regions, billed to the LLC. Each provider gets its OWN extdeps module under the external-decomposition rule - one independently versioned upstream, one authority, no generic hub enumerating providers - carrying its cited pricing units (storage per GB-month, class A/B operations, egress) and its published quota and rate limits, each with the source URL and the date read. The bucket IDENTITY and the ENROLLED SCOPE are declared here, not left implicit: which bucket is the durable origin, what is admitted to it, and under whose credential. NOT owed by this item: choosing between the two, which is a cost decision the pricing modules make derivable rather than a preference to be asserted now.",
  depends_on: no_deps,
  relates_to: ["strategy.compute_fabric_model", "strategy.ci_storage_tiering"],
  item_relations: no_item_relations,
  status: InProgress { note: "2026-09-19 CORRECTION: THE 2026-09-10 NOTE BELOW MEASURED THE ACCOUNT AND ITS API TOKENS, NOT R2 ITSELF. The R2 subscription had never been activated and the bucket gunbai-fabric-origin did not exist, so every signed request to the origin endpoint failed its TLS handshake (same failure from the session container, srv1 and a BuildBuddy runner; an invented account id failed identically). On 2026-09-19 the operator activated R2 ($0 free tier) and created gunbai-fabric-origin in the dashboard (Standard class, public access disabled, default jurisdiction). Then, executed: tools.fabric_m0_origin_object_probe fetch_absent exit 0 (signed 404 for an unwritten key); gunbc.cloudflare.r2_token_mint_run run_object_write minted the write token (stored as version 1 of cloudflare-r2-origin-write-token); with that pin (public gunbc#11713) roundtrip exit 0. STILL OPEN: bucket creation and the R2-enabled check are not modelled, so this gap could recur unnoticed; the fleet principal's grants on the write secret are unconverged (the converge entries need gcloud). PREVIOUS NOTE FOLLOWS -- 2026-09-10: ACCOUNTS EXIST AT BOTH PROVIDERS and the Cloudflare half is measured rather than assumed. Account 5f71db675ad3e94c16a3d5c159d16298; a bootstrap API token is in fleet custody at version 1 of cloudflare-account-api-token-bootstrap, pinned to that exact version rather than latest. Read LIVE from the account through the modeled path on 2026-09-10: the bootstrap token carries Account API Tokens Write, which is the group the mint model was written for; and the WRITE gap is closed with an OBSERVED id rather than a guessed one - Workers R2 Storage Bucket Item Write, bucket-scoped. THE CLAUSE THAT FOLLOWED THIS ON 2026-09-10 -- 'so a durable origin CAN put' -- IS FALSE AND IS RETRACTED HERE RATHER THAN QUIETLY DELETED, because it licensed a wrong inference in a dispatched brief that then had to be retracted. OBSERVING A PERMISSION GROUP ID IS NOT A CAPABILITY. It does not establish that a token carrying it was minted, placed in custody, bound to the origin, or exercised. The frontier row forbids the inference in its own terms: cloudflare_permission_group_observation_frontier_rows dissolves only when extdeps.cloudflare.r2 DECLARES a bucket-item write grant built from the observed id AND a gunbc entry MINTS a token carrying it, and it says a witness that the id was observed does not fire it. VERIFIED AT PUBLIC MAIN 2026-09-12: extdeps.cloudflare.r2 carries workers_r2_storage_bucket_item_read_permission_group_id, r2_bucket_item_read_permission_group and r2_object_read_grant, and NO WRITE GRANT CONSTRUCTOR EXISTS ANYWHERE IN dag/. DurableOriginBucket carries a read_credential field and no writer. So this sentence did not merely lag the world -- IT CONTRADICTED THE MODULE IT DEPENDS ON, whose own prose already states that the write half lands as an observation in the observing layer and not as a grant. The read id already pinned in the public repo verified correct against the same listing. Backblaze account/key 6f38e5a145da. OUTSTANDING before Done: the two extdeps modules, the bucket identity and enrolled scope, and the executed token mint all sat on gunbc#10925, WHICH MERGED 2026-09-10 at 13:48Z after the request-changes on its bucket roster was addressed. THE PREVIOUS SENTENCE HERE SAID IT WAS UNMERGED AND WAS STALE WITHIN HOURS, which is the concrete harm a transcribed status carries: a reader plans around work that is already done, or redoes it. What remains open is therefore NOT the branch - it is whether the declarations that landed are the ones this item's exit criterion requires, which is a question about content and has to be answered by reading them. B2 published rates stay UNAVAILABLE - nothing observed retires that. This item is not Done while the declarations live only on a branch." },
}

data item_fabric_m0: PlanItem = PlanItem {
  id: "fabric-m0",
  workstream: StorageFabric,
  milestone: M1InternalVertical,
  rank: 10,
  min_calendar_days: 14,
  active_effort_days: 14,
  execution_mode: AgentParallel,
  exit_criterion: "M0 fabric per the reviewed sequence: per-node disposable CAS cache, one zero-egress durable origin, digest verification on fill, hit/miss/bytes receipts flowing, durable-commit gate (job success only after required artifact/receipt commit). No peer mesh. RECUT 2026-09-19 FROM MODELLED TO EXECUTED (docs/plans/software-delivery-map.md): the model is complete and UNCONSUMED. gunbc.fabric_m0_commit, gunbc.fabric_m0_completion and gunbc.cloudflare.r2_origin_object are imported only by witness tests under test/claim and by three instrument probes -- tools.cas_store_live_probe, tools.fabric_m0_origin_object_probe and tools.fabric_m0_origin_readback_probe -- and NO JOB PATH REACHES ANY OF THEM. TWO CONJUNCTS ARE THEREFORE ADDED AND NEITHER IS NEW MODELLING. (a) THE THREE PROBES ARE RUN AGAINST THE REAL BUCKET AND THEIR RECEIPTS COMMITTED: each is already an entry point and none has a recorded run, so this costs execution rather than authorship. (b) A REAL JOB REACHES gunbc.fabric_m0_completion THROUGH AN IMPORT AND A CALL SITE, so the durable-commit gate is what decides that job successful. Until (b), 'durable-commit gate' names a function nothing calls, and a green witness over it establishes that the function is correct rather than that the gate exists. gunbc.build_cache_instance IS DEPLOYED on the srv1-srv4 CI fleet and is NOT this: it is a build cache for gunbc's own compiles, consumed by gunbc.runner_activation, not the M0 job-path CAS.",
  depends_on: [dep(id: "storage-provider-accounts")],
  relates_to: ["strategy.compute_fabric_model"],
  item_relations: no_item_relations,
  status: InProgress { note: "2026-09-10 REFRESH -- the previous note said gunbc#10641 was open in draft. IT MERGED 2026-09-08, and planning from the stale note would have rebuilt what exists. LANDED: the durable-COMPLETION authority (gunbc.fabric_m0_completion admit_job_publication, total over four outcomes, with F0..F6 as gate predicates and 14 mutation-controlled witnesses). Its ordering is the load-bearing part -- the computation verdict is read FIRST and short-circuits, so a successful storage finalization CANNOT invert a failed build, and ReadbackUnknown is a THIRD arm because a lost acknowledgement does not establish that a write failed and an object existing does not establish it is the intended object. Also landed: gunbc#10687, the event-log root path authority that refuses on an unknown host rather than defaulting. REMAINING, AND THE TWO-TRACK SEQUENCING THIS NOTE CARRIED ON 2026-09-10 WAS WRONG. It said giving admit_job_publication a production consumer needed no origin and no cache, so it could run in parallel with the R2 mint. The fabric-M0 lane refuted that by tracing the real run path rather than by argument: the required-CI job ends at claim_executor --required-ci, where phases accumulate failures and the process exit maps to the GitHub check through floor_exit_to_check_conclusion, and NOTHING on that path constructs a CommitTransportOutcome or a ManifestReadbackObservation. So that path cannot ask admit_job_publication without one of two forbidden moves -- fabricating an origin readback, which is the laundering this item's own ceiling calls out and which is the sibling A1's whole subject, or refusing every green job. (1) THE DURABLE-COMMIT GATE IS THEREFORE GATED ON THE WRITE MINT -- a bucket-item WRITE grant plus a token carrying it, exercised -- exactly as the origin binding is. The READ mint is done (gunbc#10947); naming this gate an undifferentiated 'executed mint' would now read as satisfied, which is the stale-status failure this note's 2026-09-12 correction exists to end. (2) SO IS the origin binding itself, then digest verification on fill. THE ONLY GENUINELY UNBLOCKED WORK IS origin-readback discipline as a construction, which is in flight. 2026-09-12 CORRECTION, AND THE SENTENCE THIS REPLACES WAS STALE WITHIN TWO DAYS: it said the executed R2 token mint was the SINGLE critical-path item for this item, so it slipped the whole milestone. THE READ MINT HAS EXECUTED. gunbc#10947 merged 2026-09-10 and retired its Create frontier rows; cloudflare_r2_token_mint_frontier_rows is now an EMPTY LIST, which that module states is the membership of a retired population rather than a missing declaration; bucket gunbai-fabric-origin is allocated to FabricDurableOrigin in gunbc.cloudflare.r2_origin; and fabric_durable_origin_read_secret_version is 1. WHAT REMAINS FOR THE ORIGIN IS THE WRITE HALF, WHICH IS A DIFFERENT AND UNBUILT THING: a bucket-item WRITE grant plus a token mint carrying it, exercised by a self-staging GET. Read access does not imply it -- see the storage-provider-accounts correction below, where exactly that inference was written down and is false. ORIGIN SCOPE, RECORDED AS THE FABRIC-M0 LANE'S RULING AND NOT AS A DERIVED FACT (lane judgment, 2026-09-12): M0's exit calls for ONE zero-egress durable origin, while storage-provider-accounts' exit requires accounts and cited pricing at BOTH providers and Backblaze B2's published rates stand UNAVAILABLE. The lane has ruled that M0's origin is R2 ONLY, and that storage-provider-accounts is therefore PARTIALLY DISCHARGED for M0's purposes -- neither struck, nor converted into an obligation to implement two origins. It is written here rather than left in a lane's pull-request body so that a later reader cannot answer it by drift; it is carried as an attributed judgment because a lane's ruling laundered into a derived fact is the failure one layer above the two corrections beside it. And the missing capability is named rather than the artifact: a job-ending that already possesses the run's Work, the attempt's commit transport, and an INDEPENDENT origin readback of the commit manifest, deciding the check conclusion from the returned JobPublication. (3) ONLY THEN the per-node disposable CAS cache -- no RAID, no scrub, no rebuild, media telemetry plus auto-cull plus spare pool -- and the hit/miss/bytes receipts, which under std.materialization_ladder ARE the cache's economic justification rather than telemetry beside it: a provider is an optimization only when measured total serving cost is below recomputation, so if the receipts say it does not pay, the honest outcome is to say so. THE SEQUENCE IS NOT ARBITRARY: gunbc#10641 built the completion contract before any cache on the reasoning that a cache accelerates a contract and cannot supply one, and the remainder inherits that. TWO CEILINGS, unchanged and named rather than assumed: computed digests exist today ONLY through a shell realization over a file path (sha256sum), with no in-substrate bytes-to-digest, which one lane confirmed is a ceiling and not a blocker; and the digested file at commit must be the ORIGIN READBACK OWN OUTPUT, never a cache copy, or a valid computation over locally-sourced bytes launders a cache-read refusal into a confirmation. NO PEER MESH is a scope wall in the exit criterion, not an oversight. STORAGE ACCOUNTS ARE NO LONGER THE BLOCKER they were: both provider accounts now exist and a write-capable permission group is observed -- see storage-provider-accounts -- so what gates the origin is THE WRITE MINT -- the read mint has executed and the write grant does not exist -- and not the operator." },
}

// FABRIC SWITCH 100G CONVERGENCE FOLLOW-UP. The CRS812 fabric legs still link at 50G. The QSFP56
// host ends were recoded to NVIDIA(ETH) and now advertise 100GBASE-CR2 (gunbc: EEPROM byte 192
// 0x0B->0x40, mstlink Supported Cable Speed 100G_2X), but no bilateral 100G link trains against the
// still-Generic-coded QSFP-DD switch end -- leading hypothesis is that end coding, NOT proven. A
// precise, evidenced question is with FS (Nia); reply expected in a few days. This node exists so
// the follow-up is not lost: once FS answers (recode the DD end, or the dual-compat cable, or a
// config), FIX the modeling and finish the converge path.
data item_fabric_switch_100g: PlanItem = PlanItem {
  id: "fabric-switch-100g",
  workstream: StorageFabric,
  milestone: M1InternalVertical,
  rank: 10,
  min_calendar_days: 5,
  active_effort_days: 5,
  execution_mode: AgentParallel,
  exit_criterion: "The eight CRS812 fabric legs train at 100GBASE-CR2 end to end (host and switch both report the negotiated 100G, not one end local link-ok), driven through the MODELED converge path being built in gunbc (the switch response DECODE merged -- wire records to typed readings; the live REST fetch and the converge apply are still in flight), not ad-hoc curl. Requires: FS answer on whether the QSFP-DD switch end needs coding (or the dual-compat cable); then the converge apply (switch REST plus host mstlink set grant) grounded in the FEC/autoneg config that actually trains 100G; then fabric_switch_observed updated to the converged state.",
  depends_on: no_deps,
  relates_to: ["strategy.compute_fabric_model"],
  item_relations: no_item_relations,
  status: InProgress { note: "BLOCKED ON ONE OPERATOR TEST, NOT ON FS -- see the 2026-09-21 entry below, which supersedes the earlier reading of this item as waiting on a reply. Host recode confirmed and carried on the modeled carrier (gunbc.spark.fabric_switch_observed spark-a3ee row = post-recode 0x40); the switch was read for the first time and its lanes force-tested; NO 100G link trained under any tried config (autoneg-both or forced-both via mstlink, all switch FEC modes), and RouterOS reported auto-init-failed / eeprom-checksum-bad on the Generic-coded QSFP-DD end. The isolating test is a substitution control (dual-compat cable or a known-good 100G-CR2 endpoint pair), and the evidenced question is with FS. 2026-09-18: FS replied asking for the forced-speed / autoneg-off breakout configuration and whether the ConnectX-7 was operationally up; one operator-approved retest of that exact configuration on the srv5 leg left the host in Polling with no carrier (100% ping loss) while the switch read link-ok/100Gbps, the leg was restored and verified at 50G, and the redacted evidence packet went back to FS the same day (owner steps fabric-fs-evidence-dispatch, fabric-fs-reply-wait). 2026-09-21: FS REPLIED AND NAMED NO CAUSE. No configuration error was identified in the packet, no recode of the QSFP-DD switch end was ordered and no replacement cable was offered; FS asked for one further test instead, so this item is NO LONGER BLOCKED ON FS -- it is blocked on us. The reply is carried by strategy.vendor_correspondence fs_fabric_100g_retest_request and the test by owner step fabric-fs-fec-auto-retest. THE ONLY NEW VARIABLE IN IT IS FEC: the switch-side configuration in their screenshot is the one already executed on 2026-09-18, and what changes is fec-mode=auto on the switch with the ConnectX-7 returned to Auto for both speed and FEC. That cell is untested because every configuration tried so far was symmetric, and it is also asymmetric in the direction that previously produced No-partner-detected on the host, so a failure there reads on FS procedure as much as on the cable. FS also asked whether any other 400G QSFP-DD port is available for a cross-test; none is held. THE TEST RAN THE SAME DAY and produced the first candidate cause that is not about the cable: no 100G link (switch link-ok/100Gbps on its own side, host still Active at 50G with RS(528,514), 0 percent loss, restored and verified), and the FEC data FS asked for shows the ConnectX-7 accepting RS-FEC(544,514) ONLY at 100G_2X while the CRS812 fec-mode admits only fec74, fec91, auto and off and resolves auto to fec91, which is RS(528,514). Measured: the two capability sets and the resolved mode. Inferred, and put to FS as the question this item now waits on: that their disjointness at 100G_2X is the cause. IF IT HOLDS, THE TWO REMEDIES THIS ITEM HAS BEEN ORGANISED AROUND BOTH FALL -- neither a recode of the QSFP-DD end nor a replacement cable can produce a 100G link on this pairing -- so the substitution control is re-ranked below the RS-544 question rather than remaining the next step. Receipt: owner_action receipt_fs_fabric_fec_auto_result; run detail in the public docs/plans/fabric-switch-actuation-log.md. gunbc PRs: #11504 merged; #11524 and #11525 in review." },
}

data item_runner_canary: PlanItem = PlanItem {
  id: "runner-canary",
  workstream: RunnerSoftware,
  milestone: M1InternalVertical,
  rank: 10,
  min_calendar_days: 3,
  active_effort_days: 3,
  execution_mode: AgentParallel,
  exit_criterion: "The control-plane canary, split from the oversized runner-path item (analyst rank-1 schedule risk): GitHub App + workflow_job webhook -> JIT ephemeral runner in a per-job microVM on the canary host -> one real job completes -> receipt with metered vCPU-minutes -> environment destroyed. Lifecycle hardening is runner-lifecycle (M2). SHARPENED 2026-09-19: THE JOB THAT RAN AND THE PATH THAT IS MODELLED ARE DIFFERENT PROGRAMS, and this exit is about the second. gunbc.runner.runner_first_job_receipt records a real job completing -- receipt_subject_run, actions run 34086151842, conclusion success -- with every link of execution_chain observed rather than inferred, and the SAME module records that it ran a HAND-BUILT image: runner_artifact_model_disagreement, the modelled row naming 2.336.0 while 2.337.0 ran, caught by a human reading a job log because the comparator that would decide it, gunbc.runner_microvm_boot_probe boot_probe_verdict, was never invoked on that path. So this item closes only when A JOB RUNS THROUGH THE MODELLED GUEST IMAGE WITH boot_probe_verdict INVOKED, and when the two halves the receipt does not carry are present: the webhook arrival, which is webhook-ingress-durable-record, and the METERED RECEIPT, whose chain is ROOTED IN A WITNESS TEST RATHER THAN IN A JOB: gunbc.runner.runner_usage_receipt IS imported by gunbc.runner.runner_teardown_receipt, whose own only importer is test.claim.runner.runner_canary_receipt_witness_test, so no executing route reaches metering. CORRECTED 2026-09-19 from 'it has NONE anywhere', which was produced by a grep for a module path that does not exist -- dag/gunbc/runner/ declares modules BOTH as gunbc.runner_* and as gunbc.runner.runner_*, so the directory does not determine the name (DESIGN section 3: paths are discriminators, not gospel). The remaining work is one link further out and smaller than that sentence implied.",
  depends_on: no_deps,
  relates_to: ["strategy.ci_alpha"],
  item_relations: [RemainderLivesOn { of: "runner-lifecycle", why: "Lifecycle hardening is an M2 remainder; the canary can close without it." }],
  status: InProgress { note: "ONE REAL JOB NOW COMPLETES: GitHub Actions run 34086151842 executed to success in a per-job microVM on the Mt. Collins host (gunbc#10733, main c9ef79fdeea) -- host boots its own EFI-stub kernel from BMC media, the jailer drops privilege (CapEff/Prm/Inh/Amb zero, NoNewPrivs=1, Seccomp=2) and execs Firecracker v1.16.1 in place, the guest runs under KVM on kernel 6.1.128 against a host on 6.12.108, and the runner registers from inside the guest. Containment was asserted BY THE JOB rather than trusted from the host receipt: a step opened /dev/tcp to the BMC controlling its own machine and required failure, and two observers with no shared instrument agree -- GitHub log plus the host guest-to-bmc rule carrying exactly 3 dropped packets, the SYN and its two retransmits. forward-default-drop stayed at ZERO across 567 established packets of runner-chosen traffic. Since then: two VMs on one host, and a 5832-file checkout running node v24.19.0 inside the guest. THREE CONJUNCTS REMAIN. (a) GitHub App to workflow_job webhook via fleet convergence -- the host currently asks for a JIT config at boot and THE ENDPOINT SERVING IT IS UNAUTHENTICATED, recorded in gunbc#10733 as a real gap rather than left in a shell script. (b) Receipt with metered vCPU-minutes -- not established. (c) Environment destroyed in the SAME TRANSACTION as the mint -- and zero-surviving-jailer is NOT evidence for it, because the stock jailer execs into Firecracker in place on the same PID; teardown must bind to the attempt launch/exec identity set including the BusyBox timeout watcher. The srv1 kvm-group gap no longer blocks this item: the canary executes on Mt. Collins, not srv1. 2026-09-16 (eager-owl-205): conjuncts (b) and (c) have their PRODUCERS on public main (gunbc#11177: RunnerUsageReceipt with exact fractional vCPU-minutes over the jailer-launch-to-VMM-reap duration; teardown receipt joining the launch inventory to a separate observer's present-before/absent-after readings) with fixture witnesses only -- LIVE EVIDENCE PENDING, and the same PR records why: no authorized host-shell/boot-image path on the driveless unit at the time. Conjunct (a), the unauthenticated JIT endpoint, is untouched. The path back to a live job is therefore: mint the unit-1 subject + SecretRef (bmc_secure frontier) so the modeled boot route authenticates -> re-attach the host image as virtual media and boot the restored 16-module host (first Linux boot since the memory change; closes hw-first-host's EDAC pass in the same session) -> run one job and capture #11177's usage and teardown receipts live -> authenticate the JIT endpoint. Four sessions, the first two operator-attended; nothing in it is research." },
}

data item_cohort_qualified: PlanItem = PlanItem {
  id: "cohort-qualified",
  workstream: AcquisitionMarketing,
  milestone: M1InternalVertical,
  rank: 10,
  min_calendar_days: 14,
  active_effort_days: 14,
  execution_mode: ExternalLead,
  exit_criterion: "STARTS NOW - November customers cannot be manufactured after October dogfood. THE DISCOVERY METHOD IS A SEARCH, WITH TWO CLAIMS ABOUT IT WITHDRAWN. Repositories running on a third-party CI provider are ENUMERABLE, because the provider label appears verbatim in .github/workflows, and their workflows are readable, so the arm64 and container questions below are answered by READING rather than by interviewing. What that label does NOT establish was overstated on first writing and is corrected here. It does not establish ARM: a provider offering both architectures selects by SUFFIXED labels, and only the arm-suffixed ones are evidence of an arm64 workload - an unsuffixed label is evidence of the opposite. It does not establish PAID SPEND either, because free tiers and credits exist, so willingness to pay stays an interview question rather than a search result. The residual interview is therefore LARGER than first claimed: org-owner availability, secrets and private registries, which deploy jobs must be excluded, and whether the account is actually paying. The requirement: 3-5 prospects identified and workload-qualified (arm64 compatibility, Docker/service-container needs, privileged-mode assumptions, private registries, secrets, excluded deploy jobs, job memory/disk ceilings, untrusted-PR behavior), org-owner availability confirmed, expected usage and dates committed.",
  depends_on: no_deps,
  relates_to: ["strategy.ci_alpha"],
  item_relations: no_item_relations,
  status: NotStarted,
}

data item_app_install_rehearsal: PlanItem = PlanItem {
  id: "external-app-install-rehearsal",
  workstream: RunnerSoftware,
  milestone: M1InternalVertical,
  rank: 20,
  min_calendar_days: 3,
  active_effort_days: 3,
  execution_mode: ExternalLead,
  exit_criterion: "The real public GitHub App installed into an external friendly org via direct install link (Marketplace review is NOT on the path) and an org-level JIT runner created there: the receipt names org, approving owner, granted permissions (incl. org self-hosted-runners write), selected repos, runner group, and one completed test job. The real external lead is ORG-OWNER APPROVAL, and this rehearses it.",
  depends_on: [dep(id: "runner-canary")],
  relates_to: ["strategy.ci_product_surface"],
  item_relations: no_item_relations,
  status: NotStarted,
}

data item_dogfood_started: PlanItem = PlanItem {
  id: "dogfood-started",
  workstream: EconomicsQa,
  milestone: M1InternalVertical,
  rank: 30,
  min_calendar_days: 1,
  active_effort_days: 1,
  execution_mode: AgentParallel,
  exit_criterion: "gunbc's own CI runs on the canary host through the runner-canary path - the two-week observation clock STARTS. Split from window completion because the calendar minimum cannot be parallelized away and integration defects may restart part of the window.",
  depends_on: [dep(id: "hw-first-host"), dep(id: "boot-minimum"), dep(id: "fabric-m0"), dep(id: "runner-canary"), CompletionRequires { of: "webhook-ingress-durable-record", why: "THE CLOCK MEASURES A SERVICE, NOT A DEMONSTRATION. A two-week observation window over a path where each job arrives because the operator started it measures the operator, not the runner. The ingress is what makes an unattended job possible, so it is a completion edge and not a start edge." }],
  relates_to: ["strategy.ci_alpha"],
  item_relations: no_item_relations,
  status: NotStarted,
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// M1b - INTERNAL S0 PROOF (2026-10-15): two uninterrupted dogfood weeks complete; all four
// machines admitted or explicitly refused; receipt streams and failure dispositions live.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

data item_hw_4_population: PlanItem = PlanItem {
  id: "hw-4-population",
  workstream: Hardware,
  milestone: M1bInternalS0Proof,
  rank: 20,
  min_calendar_days: 21,
  active_effort_days: 21,
  execution_mode: OperatorExclusive,
  exit_criterion: "Units 2-4 through the same intake in parallel with the canary's software work: each ADMITTED (receipt module) or explicitly REFUSED with the defect named - a four-way disposition, not a four-way pass assumption. RATIONALE, ASKED FOR AND WORTH CARRYING (operator, 2026-09-10: \"i don't know which server was taken through what\"). THAT SENTENCE IS THE ITEM'S JUSTIFICATION, not an aside: if nobody can say which unit passed which step, then no unit has been qualified -- there is an impression of progress and no receipt. This item exists so admission is per-unit and legible, which buys three things. It prevents a defective unit reaching the fleet and being diagnosed later as a software fault, which is the expensive failure. It produces the four-way disposition the criterion demands, so a REFUSED unit is a named defect that can be returned or reworked while the vendor window is open rather than a machine quietly set aside. And it gives node-burnin-protocol its subject: that item writes the protocol, this one is the first population it runs against. The twenty invoiced units make it larger, not different.",
  depends_on: [dep(id: "hw-first-host")],
  relates_to: ["strategy.ci_node_build"],
  item_relations: [ProvidesSubject { of: "node-burnin-protocol", why: "This item is the first population the burn-in protocol runs against; it does not wait on the protocol being written." }],
  status: NotStarted,
}

// USE-CASE SCOUTING (operator direction 2026-09-17: "we basically need to invest in scouting for
// use cases before year end", "my goal is to align our own use cases with the market"). THIS IS
// NOT public-workload-census AND NOT customer-workload-profile, and the difference is why it is a
// separate item: the census's subject is a CI workflow JOB and cannot represent a remote-execution
// workload, while customer-workload-profile depends on cohort-qualified and first-external-customer
// and therefore cannot run before customers exist -- which is exactly when "what should we sell"
// has to be answered. THE Q2 RECUT IS WHAT MAKES THIS THE YEAR-END WORK: with the wholesale
// production programme moved to M5, finding WHICH two or three customers the residence serves is
// the critical path, and scouting needs no rack.
// THE AGENT-WORKSPACE DOGFOOD (operator direction 2026-09-17: "get my session dashboard onto this
// architecture as a proof of concept - i can deal with the failovers myself"). DISTINCT FROM
// dogfood-started, which is gunbc's own CI on the canary host through the runner-canary path: that
// is the BUILD class, this is the AGENT-WORKSPACE class, different workload, different consumer,
// different contract. Both are dogfood and neither substitutes for the other.
//
// STAGED, NOT CUT OVER, AND THE REASON IS THE REPOSITORY'S OWN DOCTRINE. A working environment is a
// gap-intolerant boundary, and for those the replacement rule keeps the staged form: build in
// shadow, run in parallel, then one transition. Moving primary sessions onto a host that has booted
// Linux once would put the operator's own productivity on the critical path of an unproven
// substrate, and a proof of concept that costs its author their working day gets abandoned for
// reasons unrelated to whether it worked.
//
// THE OPERATOR ABSORBS THE INTERRUPTIONS DELIBERATELY, which is what makes him the right first
// tenant: the cost of a wrong failover contract lands internally, where it teaches, instead of on a
// customer, where it churns. The exit therefore COUNTS interruptions rather than requiring zero.
data item_agent_workspace_dogfood: PlanItem = PlanItem {
  id: "agent-workspace-dogfood",
  workstream: OpsMachineHealth,
  milestone: M3YearEndGate,
  rank: 45,
  min_calendar_days: 21,
  active_effort_days: 10,
  execution_mode: AgentParallel,
  exit_criterion: "THE OPERATOR'S OWN AGENT WORKSPACES SERVED FROM OWNED HARDWARE FOR TWO CONSECUTIVE WEEKS, with a real repository and representative Claude Code and Codex CLI sessions, and the four domains separated: an immutable digest-addressed root, a durable per-workspace volume, a tenant-scoped secret path, and disposable scratch. RECONCILED 2026-09-18 with the acceptance rehearsal a side-chat review proposed as a separate item; folded in here rather than minted beside it, because two overlapping dogfood items would each be half-satisfied. THE DESTRUCTION TEST IS NOT A VM RESTART: destroy the RESIDENCE HOST and reconstruct the workspace ON A SECOND ADMITTED HOST THAT READS NOTHING FROM THE FIRST - a reconstruction that depends on the old host being reachable proves nothing about host loss. ONE ACTIVE WRITER IS ENFORCED before the workspace attaches elsewhere, because two executors on one volume corrupt the repository and a host that appears dead is not necessarily dead. THE VOLUME MUST CARRY: repositories and worktrees including uncommitted edits; the agent home with settings and RESUMABLE SESSION HISTORY, measured 2026-09-17 at 150 transcript files and 674 MB for one machine; Codex resume state; dotfiles and agent instructions; git identity. IT MUST NOT CARRY credentials: those are REACQUIRED through the secret path, so a reconstruction that works because an API key sat in the volume FAILS this item. Build outputs, downloads and language-server indexes are expected to be lost. A SUBSTANTIAL BUILD IS DISPATCHED OFF THE SEAT during the window, since the memory envelope only holds if builds leave. FOUR MEASUREMENTS ARE RECORDED: customer-observed reconnect and resume time; the volume's metadata latency, locking, atomic-rename and durability under the interactive load, against the baseline that one git status over the gunbc repository is about 6,900 metadata operations and 0.07s locally; the per-workspace envelope under a tenant that builds; and the interruption count. PASS BOUNDARY: a host failure MAY lose an active turn, an in-flight command, or an external effect of unknown idempotence, and MAY NOT lose an acknowledged file change or resumable session state; only the second fails the item. STAGED, NOT CUT OVER: a parallel workspace runs first and the primary moves only after it survives two weeks. This is the replayed specimen that can settle the persistent-agent-workspace row's ShapeObligationUnread in strategy.served_workload_frontier.",
  depends_on: [CompletionRequires { of: "durable-workspace-volume", why: "The exit is a TWENTY-ONE DAY OBSERVATION and the volume is a BUILD. Folding the construction into the window is how a three-week exit silently becomes a five-week one; the clock cannot start against a volume that does not exist." }, dep(id: "hw-first-host"), dep(id: "boot-minimum")],
  relates_to: ["strategy.served_workload_frontier", "strategy.home_hosting", "strategy.fleet_convergence"],
  item_relations: no_item_relations,
  status: NotStarted,
}

data item_use_case_scouting: PlanItem = PlanItem {
  id: "use-case-scouting",
  workstream: AcquisitionMarketing,
  milestone: M3YearEndGate,
  rank: 10,
  min_calendar_days: 14,
  active_effort_days: 7,
  execution_mode: AgentParallel,
  exit_criterion: "AT LEAST THREE CANDIDATE CLASSES IN strategy.served_workload_frontier, each carrying its interface, SERVICE SHAPE, atomic unit, contract, SHAPE OBLIGATION, architecture fit, incumbent, dogfood standing, replay standing and kill condition -- the shape and its obligation were added when one universal promise turned out to fit remote build execution and not a persistent workspace, and an earlier cut of this brief still demanded a five-property contract the type no longer has - AND AT LEAST ONE SETTLED IN EITHER DIRECTION, admitted or structurally excluded, because a roster where everything is pending records no scouting. THE ADMISSION RULE IS DERIVED, NOT AUTHORED: THE ADMISSION RULE IS NOT RESTATED HERE: read qualifies_for_frontier, because every prose copy of it in this corpus has gone stale within a day of being written. What the brief does state, because the fold cannot: admission is DERIVED and admission_standing_is_earned refuses a row claiming more than it allows. WHAT IS DELIBERATELY NOT REQUIRED HERE: expected margin, utilisation and operational burden. Those cannot be answered before a specimen is replayed, so demanding them at scouting time would produce projections typed as readings (DESIGN section 4d). THE FIRST QUESTION TO ANSWER IS THE ARCHITECTURE ONE on remote-build execution: our own remote-build demand is linux/amd64 and the fleet is Ampere arm64, so 'we are our own customer' is unproven for this supply until our own workspace is built on one Ampere host and compared. That is one host and one afternoon, it needs no rack, and it either grounds the dogfood claim or kills the class.",
  depends_on: no_deps,
  relates_to: ["strategy.served_workload_frontier", "strategy.workload_benchmark_suite", "strategy.demand_utilization"],
  item_relations: no_item_relations,
  status: InProgress {
    note: "The carrier landed with two rows: remote-build execution (AdmissibleOnCondition - architecture unresolved, no replayed specimen, no buyer who is not us) and customer-database hosting (OutsideFrontier, IntrinsicallyIncompatible - durable state availability IS the product, so it is a different service class rather than a workload awaiting modernisation). A third class and the arm64 build comparison are the open work.",
  },
}

data item_public_workload_census: PlanItem = PlanItem {
  id: "public-workload-census",
  workstream: EconomicsQa,
  milestone: M1InternalVertical,
  rank: 10,
  min_calendar_days: 5,
  active_effort_days: 5,
  execution_mode: AgentParallel,
  exit_criterion: "A small VERSIONED population of public workflow JOBS inspected - jobs, not repositories, because compatibility is job-scoped and an Arm publishing job proves nothing about whether the build and tests run natively. Each candidate records repository and source revision, workflow/job/matrix identity, DECLARED provider and architecture, OBSERVED run evidence or its absence, workload commands, cache mechanisms, resource requirements, external effects, and replay-admission gaps. Two or three complementary workloads are selected; rejected and unresolved candidates stay visible with their reasons. FIVE PROMOTIONS ARE FORBIDDEN and they are what this item exists to prevent: an x64 label may not become Arm evidence, a skipped or failed test may not become a successful baseline, an unobserved cache may not become warm, provider use may not become verified spend, and a benchmark result may not become trial or outreach authorization. Each candidate therefore carries SEPARATE fields for provider declaration, observed execution, replay admission, commercial interest and trial authorization rather than one qualified Boolean. Two admission rules bind the replay itself: public visibility is not a licence, so the source, dependencies and data are checked before replay; and external mutations - registry pushes, cloud role assumption, deployment - are removed from BOTH realizations, which makes the result a build/test replay DERIVED from the workflow and not an execution of the original pipeline. No outreach is authorized by anything in this item, and code-search results may not become unsolicited contact.",
  depends_on: no_deps,
  relates_to: ["strategy.ci_acquisition", "extdeps.pricing.ubicloud"],
  item_relations: no_item_relations,
  status: InProgress { note: "gunbc#11179 open as of 2026-09-13, GitHub CLEAN. Observed provider is a ProviderReading rather than a DeclaredProviderStanding; declared_architecture_is_arm deleted so UNRESOLVED is no longer fused with NOT-ARM; the correctness join keys on WorkflowJobRun.run_attempt rather than assuming one attempt per run. Not Done: the exit criterion is a versioned population, not a PR. WIND-DOWN, 2026-09-14: gunbc#11179 is AT THE FLOOR at head 7375c912711 -- CLEAN, all four required lanes SUCCESS, one approval -- and lands from the merge queue on side-chat APPROVE, not by more work. The zero-approvals clause this replaces was true when written." }
}

data item_incumbent_head_to_head: PlanItem = PlanItem {
  id: "incumbent-head-to-head",
  workstream: EconomicsQa,
  milestone: M1bInternalS0Proof,
  rank: 30,
  min_calendar_days: 7,
  active_effort_days: 7,
  execution_mode: AgentParallel,
  exit_criterion: "One ADMITTED workload from public-workload-census executed on the srv1 canary AND on an authorized incumbent account, using the same identified source and workload contract, with any workflow adaptation recorded and applied to BOTH sides. Both sides must satisfy the selected correctness checks: a fast failure is not a speed win, and a job whose tests did not run has not been compared. THE MAINTAINER'S OWN RUN HISTORY IS SCREENING, NEVER THE BASELINE - its cache contents, account settings and environment are unknown, so both sides run in our own controlled account. COLD AND WARM ARE THREE CONDITIONS, NOT TWO, because the incumbent starts a fresh VM per job AND restores a remote cache by default, so a fresh worker is not a cold cache: logical cold is confirmed MISSES on the relevant caches; remote-warm-on-a-fresh-worker is the condition that actually tests an ephemeral-worker design; and a representative incremental change - parent commit populates, child commit does real work - keeps the verdict off an unchanged-source rerun. Which cache layers were controlled is recorded, because dependencies, compiler outputs, image layers and artifact inputs are different populations. Timing is decomposed into pre-execution wait, runner preparation, checkout, dependency install, cache restore, build and test, and required upload, read from the SPECIFIC run attempt rather than a workflow-level duration; for a multi-job workflow the customer-visible critical path is distinguished from the sum of job durations. EVERY MATERIAL GAP NAMES ITS OBSERVED STAGE, ITS ATTRIBUTION STANDING - measured cause, supported hypothesis, or unattributed - AND ITS NEXT DISCRIMINATING TEST; an earlier version of this row demanded that every gap name its cause, which is exactly the demand for premature certainty that manufactures the unsupported story it was meant to prevent. Resource allocation is matched and scratch is declared: if scratch consumes RAM it is charged to the memory budget, if it crosses the network that path is measured, and no worker drive appears as an unreported benchmark optimization. Roughly five to ten paired repetitions per condition with alternating order, individual observations reported alongside median and range, and cancellations, outages and test failures classified by a rule declared BEFORE the runs and retained in the population - not re-run until an attractive number appears. The commercial reading is COST TO OBTAIN AN EQUIVALENT VALID RESULT including failed-attempt charges, at dated tariffs, fed into the existing cost assessment rather than a new benchmark-specific cost authority: a higher rate can win by finishing sooner and a cheaper rate can lose on setup and retries. Missing evidence yields an explicit INCOMPLETE comparison, never an assumed winner, and no result here qualifies a customer or authorizes outreach. THE INCUMBENT SIDE IS A RUNNER WE OPERATE, NOT THE REPOSITORY'S OWN HISTORY, and the census made that distinction load-bearing rather than pedantic. The originating idea was to find a repository running on Ubicloud and clone it, and the observed population does not support it: of the selected workloads, the two with real correctness checks run on DEPOT and on GitHub-hosted arm runners, and the only job observed on Ubicloud Arm is the one whose baseline admission REFUSES it because no test executes. So the repository's declared and observed provider is SCREENING - it identifies an arm64 workload worth replaying - while the comparison arm is an incumbent account we open and control. Declared provider and observed provider are separate facts and neither may be promoted into the other. A consequence worth stating because it was invisible before the census: Depot, not Ubicloud, is the arm provider actually observed carrying these workloads, so the competitive set is wider than the price table's Ubicloud row and the choice of which incumbent to run against is now a decision rather than an assumption. Expectation set for the Ubicloud arm specifically: its Arm runners are Ampere Altra Q80-30, the same processor family this fleet holds, so THAT pairing measures the SERVICE PATH - cache, network, scheduling, setup - and not the silicon. No such equivalence is claimed for any other incumbent until its hardware is cited.",
  depends_on: [dep(id: "runner-canary"), dep(id: "fabric-m0")],
  relates_to: ["strategy.ci_runner_economics", "extdeps.pricing.ubicloud", "strategy.workload_benchmark_suite"],
  item_relations: [ConsumesAdmittedWork { of: "public-workload-census", why: "The comparison executes one admitted workload from the census; the census does not have to finish as a scheduling predecessor of this item's start, and adding dep() would be a new blocking claim." }],
  status: NotStarted,
}

