data item_colo_rfq: PlanItem = PlanItem {
  id: "colo-rfq",
  workstream: Hardware,
  milestone: M5Q2ColoDeployment,
  rank: 10,
  min_calendar_days: 30,
  active_effort_days: 30,
  execution_mode: ExternalLead,
  exit_criterion: "All-in RFQ (the reviewed 17-line schema) issued NOW to the census candidates; responses modeled as CostQuoted rows carrying quote validity, delivery/turn-up lead time, available capacity, deposit, and expansion rights - not only price. NOTHING SIGNED.",
  depends_on: no_deps,
  relates_to: ["strategy.colo_market", "strategy.site_requirements", "strategy.wholesale_batch_floor"],
  item_relations: no_item_relations,
  status: InProgress { note: "RFQ issued 2026-09-14 by the operator through each facility's inquiry form to the five census candidates in strategy.wholesale_batch_floor quote_shortlist - two certified at the 16 kW commit by a published air floor (DataBank LGA4 and LGA3), three unresolved by the published claim because no cooling medium is named, of which Digital Fortress is conditional (its 15 kW floor sits below the commit): DataBank LGA4 and LGA3 Orangeburg, Iron Mountain NJE-1 Edison, Netrality 401 N Broad Philadelphia, Digital Fortress PNJ Piscataway. WHAT WENT OUT IS THE EIGHT-LINE ASK (wholesale_batch_floor rfq_asks), NOT the reviewed 17-line schema this item's exit criterion names - the earlier note said 17 and was wrong. The remainder is owed as an addendum (wholesale_batch_floor rfq_addendum_asks: A+B independence through the plant, PDU handoff, cabinet depth for the 857 mm chassis, air-cooled capacity in writing at 16 kW, transit billing method and burst, routed-vs-attached /29, dock and staging, MRC start date, insurance wording, escalators and contiguous-cabinet rights) and goes to the named sales engineer each facility assigns. First follow-up is a named owner within three business days (by 2026-09-17), not the two-week check; 2026-09-28 is the no-response escalation. A 15 kW response is a CONDITIONAL candidate, not an automatic fallback: it leaves 1,350 W above the 21-node planning load and nothing for an on-site cache pair or switching. The item exits when responses are modeled as CostQuoted rows and the site band in wholesale_batch_floor dissolves into a Quoted arm. NETRALITY ANSWERED BY PHONE 2026-09-14 (wholesale_batch_floor netrality_response): about four weeks from an installation contract to space; the deployment is not significant for them and ten times the size would be simple. A lead time and a capacity remark, not a quote - the Quoted arm stays empty until a written quote with coverage lands; the lead time is now colo-turnup-rack-acceptance's calendar floor." },
}

