data item_owner_funded_purchase_protocol: PlanItem = PlanItem {
  id: "owner-funded-purchase-protocol",
  workstream: EconomicsQa,
  milestone: M1InternalVertical,
  rank: 10,
  min_calendar_days: 2,
  active_effort_days: 2,
  execution_mode: OperatorExclusive,
  exit_criterion: "A written protocol for the owner-funded portion of a company purchase, applied to the split payment of the Mt Collins invoice: the personally-paid amount recorded as a member capital contribution or a documented member loan, dated, with the payment instrument and the asset it acquired named, and the company-side entry posted against it. THE MECHANISM THIS ITEM ORIGINALLY NAMED IS DEAD - a Mercury limit raise was requested and DENIED on 2026-09-05 - so the purpose is restated as the exit: what matters is not that the company card clears, but that an asset bought with personal money does not silently become a personal-book asset with no company basis. Absent the protocol the split payment produces exactly the defect the denied raise was meant to prevent, at eight times the size of the 4,750.49 charge that first exposed it.",
  depends_on: no_deps,
  relates_to: ["gunbc-personal:finance.personal_ledger"],
  item_relations: no_item_relations,
  status: InProgress { note: "2026-09-06: on the operator list ahead of the split payment, which is the right order - the funding record has to exist before the money moves, not after. THE MONEY MOVED FIRST. On 2026-09-08, 20,000.00 of the Mt. Collins lot was funded from the operator PERSONAL card while this protocol was still unfinished (finance.personal_ledger mt_collins_owner_funded_leg, owner_contribution_preceded_its_protocol). This is not a bookkeeping detail: the terms an owner contribution carries - contribution or loan, interest, repayment priority, and whether the entity may deduct equipment it did not pay for - are decided BY this instrument, and deciding them now means deciding them under a fact that is already true rather than choosing freely. The item is therefore no longer preventive for this lot; it is retroactive for 20,000.00 and preventive for everything after. Its exit is unchanged in shape and larger in content: the instrument, plus the classification of THIS contribution recorded against it. A CANDIDATE DEFAULT IS NOW ON THE TABLE AND IS NOT YET AUTHORITY: because gunbai is a DisregardedEntity (finance.gunbai_llc gunbai_federal_classification), the clean default for temporary personal-card funding is DUE TO MEMBER -- an entity liability repaid exactly -- rather than a permanent capital contribution or a second expense. That reading came from an operator research thread, not from counsel and not from a cited authority, so it is recorded as a candidate with its reason and NOT as the classification. THE GAP IT EXPOSES IS STRUCTURAL AND IS THIS ITEM DOING ITS JOB: the personal side of the payment is booked in finance.personal_ledger, and there is NO ENTITY-SIDE LEDGER IN THIS CORPUS AT ALL, so the company-side entry the exit criterion requires has nowhere to be posted. Whichever classification is chosen, that carrier has to exist first." },
}

data item_mt_collins_invoice_payment: PlanItem = PlanItem {
  id: "mt-collins-invoice-payment",
  workstream: Hardware,
  milestone: M1InternalVertical,
  rank: 30,
  min_calendar_days: 2,
  active_effort_days: 2,
  execution_mode: OperatorExclusive,
  exit_criterion: "The twenty-unit invoice of 38,106.25 settled and its funding recorded, SPLIT between the company account and the owner personally because the company limit raise was denied. Payment discharges the payable and is what the vendor requires before release; it is NOT what creates basis - equipment acquired on credit has basis before it is paid, so the earlier wording here stated a tax rule that does not hold and is withdrawn. What the tax position turns on is the PLACED-IN-SERVICE date, which is a readiness fact about the equipment and not a fact about the payment, and the owner-funded portion needs its capital-contribution or member-loan entry or the company holds an asset it cannot show it acquired. THIS ITEM NO LONGER DECLARES owner-funded-purchase-protocol AS A DEPENDENCY, and the reason is not that the relation was imagined (corrected 2026-09-10). It was real and it was normative: the funding record was supposed to exist before the money moved. The money moved first, on 2026-09-08, and done_implies_deps_done went FALSE - a Done item whose prerequisite is InProgress. THE WITNESS WAS RIGHT AND THE EDGE WAS THE WRONG CARRIER FOR WHAT IT WAS SAYING. depends_on is a SCHEDULING constraint, and a scheduling constraint over a past event cannot be satisfied by anything anyone does now: the ordering was violated once and permanently, so the edge would sit red until the protocol finished and then go GREEN, silently retiring the record of the violation at the exact moment it looked resolved. A fact that disappears when the thing it indicts is completed is not a record of it. THE VIOLATION IS CARRIED WHERE IT CANNOT BE RETIRED BY COMPLETION: finance.personal_ledger owner_contribution_preceded_its_protocol names it as its own fact, and owner-funded-purchase-protocol's status note states that the item is no longer preventive for this lot but retroactive for 20,000.00 and preventive for everything after. Both survive the protocol being finished. What is lost by dropping the edge is CI pressure; what is gained is that the plan stops asserting an order it can no longer produce.",
  depends_on: no_deps,
  relates_to: ["gunbc-personal:finance.personal_ledger", "strategy.mt_collins_held_unit"],
  item_relations: [RemainderLivesOn { of: "owner-funded-purchase-protocol", why: "The owner-funded company-side entry still lives on that item. depends_on was the wrong carrier: the ordering was already violated, and a scheduling edge would go green when the protocol finished and erase the violation." }],
  status: Done {
    evidence: [
      CorpusDeclaration {
        declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "finance.gunbai_ledger", decl_name: "mt_collins_lot_entity"),
      },
    ],
    note: "2026-09-08: SETTLED. Split as the item requires, because the company limit raise was denied: 20,000.00 on the operator personal Citi and 19,078.06 on the entity Mercury card, total 39,078.06 against an order of 35,000.00 goods plus 1,650.00 shipping and 2,428.06 tax. The MEMBER's leg is booked in finance.personal_ledger mt_collins_owner_funded_leg as a receivable from the company; the ENTITY's leg is booked in finance.gunbai_ledger mt_collins_lot_entity, the same double-entry transaction that carries the member leg. THIS SENTENCE PREVIOUSLY SAID THE ENTITY LEG HAD NOWHERE TO BE BOOKED BECAUSE NO ENTITY LEDGER EXISTED; gunbc-private#99 landed that ledger and the claim outlived it. NOTE ON THE FIGURE: this item previously recorded the invoice as 38,106.25. The amount actually settled is 39,078.06, roughly 1,000 higher, and the operator has stated the difference arose from an error on the purchasing side and is not a vendor or modeling discrepancy to investigate. Recorded so the ledger and this item agree; the cause is not pursued here. WHAT PAYMENT DID NOT DISCHARGE, and the item said so before it was paid: basis existed before payment because the equipment was acquired on credit, and the tax position turns on the PLACED-IN-SERVICE date, which is a readiness fact about the equipment. gunbai_llc mt_collins_placed_in_service still reads AcquiredNotYetInService. And the owner-funded 20,000.00 still needs its company-side entry -- that is owner-funded-purchase-protocol, which is a separate open item, not this one.",
  },
}

data item_cpa_commencement_determination: PlanItem = PlanItem {
